{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund and mandate regular audits of NHS endometriosis referral and follow-up care",
        "additional_details": "In our view, too many people with suspected endometriosis experience years of pain, repeated appointments and delayed referrals, often feeling dismissed. NICE guidance sets out recommended care, but more must be done to ensure it is followed consistently. Regular audits of NHS endometriosis care, published findings and mandatory improvement plans where standards are not met could help reduce delays, improve accountability and ensure patients receive appropriate investigations, referrals and follow-up care.",
        "background": "Fund and mandate regular audits of NHS endometriosis care to ensure NHS services follow NICE guidance on referrals, investigations and follow-up for suspected endometriosis. Findings and improvement plans based on such audits should be published to improve accountability and patient care.",
